    "title": "pandas.Categorical.as_unordered — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Categorical.as_unordered#\n\n- Categorical.as_unordered()[source]#\n- Set the Categorical to be unordered. This method returns a new Categorical with the ordered attribute set to False, disabling comparison operations between categories. \n  - Returns:\n    - Categorical\n    - Unordered Categorical.\n See also \n  - `as_ordered`\n  - Set the Categorical to be ordered.\n Examples For `pandas.Series` :>>> raw_cat = pd.Categorical([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"a\"], ordered=True) >>> ser = pd.Series(raw_cat) >>> ser.cat.ordered True >>> ser = ser.cat.as_unordered() >>> ser.cat.ordered False For `pandas.CategoricalIndex` :>>> ci = pd.CategoricalIndex([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"a\"], ordered=True) >>> ci.ordered True >>> ci = ci.as_unordered() >>> ci.ordered False",
    "markdown_length": 744,
